  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ghana Horticulture Business</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The horticulture sector in Ghana, though underdeveloped, presents significant potential for economic growth and youth employment.The Netherlands embassy in Accra, Ghana seeks to catalyse systemic change by focusing on specific areas within Ghana&apos;s horticultural industry, such as open field farming for domestic markets and professionalising the sector. Dutch companies, particularly seed producers, are interested in investing in Ghana and collaborating on variety promotion, demonstrations, and training.Opportunities exist in low-tech nurseries, agricultural storage, and logistics, with future potential in greenhouses and irrigation technology. Collaboration between Ghanaian and Dutch firms, particularly in digital and sustainable solutions, offers mutual benefits.A seminar is planned to raise awareness of these opportunities and encourage Dutch businesses to engage in partnerships within the combi-track framework. The seminar will also showcase the results of ongoing projects, including the ACHI initiative, aimed at enhancing skills, sustainability, and Dutch-Ghanaian collaboration in horticulture.</narrative>
  </description>
